  "name": "pawnproof wormhole",
  "description": "Wormhole (Gardner's five by five minichess with one fixed pair of portals on the middle row, b3 and d3) with one rule added: no pawn may go through. A knight, bishop, rook, queen or king that ends its move on one end comes out one step beyond the other, in the direction it was travelling, capturing there as usual; to a pawn both ends are blocks it cannot pass or take. In Wormhole a pawn through the door lands a step from promotion with a capture on the first move, and the first player wins the race; keeping the pawns out is what makes the door a fair fight. Nobody moves the portals.",
